rence-completeness","usage":{"input_tokens":6002,"output_tokens":374,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"13f6bd0bf4f86a880af33ae2e0b1114abe1f2b8105ce6b638c432ce21eb65abd"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T1","usage":{"input_tokens":18462,"output_tokens":1168,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"746c65cfea09d04ac9461661e13a589903a93ae12fdc6ea2221f6020aaf20368"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G6","usage":{"input_tokens":20529,"output_tokens":2404,"requests":3}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the AC1 'skip when packed' option against AC3/DoD 'both shapes exercised': either drop the skip allowance and require the object be removed regardless of storage shape, or restate DoD to accept a documented skip.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["COH","E2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.07,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed'","AC3: 'proven against BOTH storage shapes — object loose, and object packed'","DoD: 'Both storage shapes exercised.'"],"finding":"AC1 permits the test to 'skip with a stated reason when the object is packed', but DoD and AC3 require BOTH storage shapes to be exercised — a skip on the packed store means the missing-object behavior is never exercised there, contradicting the other criteria.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6ab5d4554c32dad5","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC1 vs AC3 vs Definition of Done","norm_id":"nfda2c5306ac84243","priority":0.67,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor implements the skip branch on packed stores, satisfying AC1 but leaving AC3/DoD unmet","Packed-store CI runs skip the guarded behavior entirely, reproducing the original 'green run proves nothing' problem"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Change AC1 to require removal by a storage-agnostic supported route (so the missing-object condition is reached whether loose or packed), and reserve the skip only for a genuinely unreachable case with the reason recorded.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reconcile AC1's 'skip when packed' allowance with AC3's 'both storage shapes' requirement: prefer forcing a deterministic missing-object condition on packed storage (e.g. unpack the target object then unlink, or repack with the object excluded) so the fail-closed path runs in BOTH shapes rather than skipping the packed case.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.4,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC1: 'removes the object from the database by a supported route (or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed)'","AC3: 'The fix is proven against BOTH storage shapes — object loose, and object packed — rather than only the one a developer happens to have.'","Skipping on packed leaves the missing-object PinnedTicketViewError path unexercised in exactly the CI condition the plan diagnoses as the failure trigger."],"finding":"The AC permits skipping when the object is packed, but AC3 requires proving the fix against BOTH loose and packed storage. A skip means the fail-closed behaviour is never actually exercised on packed storage, so the escape hatch does not solve the stated goal (guaranteed coverage regardless of git's storage choice) — it re-introduces the same non-determinism the plan set out to remove, just inverted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c56e6be48d7a560","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (AC1 'or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed') vs AC3 ('proven against BOTH storage shapes')","norm_id":"nf8677d84adaf1062","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI packs the object before the test; test skips; the fail-closed behaviour is never verified on the storage shape that actually occurs on CI."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Resolve the skip-vs-both-shapes tension: remove the object by a route that works regardless of loose/packed storage so the fail-closed assertion actually runs in BOTH shapes, rather than skipping on the packed shape (a skip is not a proof and re-creates the 'behaviour never executed' gap).","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T5b","T6","T9","necessity","project.portability"],"criteria":["E5"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.28,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'removes the object from the database by a supported route (or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed)'","Plan: 'The fix is proven against BOTH storage shapes — object loose, and object packed'","Plan Why-it-matters: 'A green run of this test also does not prove much on any store where the object happened to be packed, since the test would have failed rather than adapted.' — a skip is likewise a non-proof on the packed shape"],"finding":"AC-1's 'or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed' escape hatch conflicts with AC-3's requirement to prove the behaviour on BOTH storage shapes: if the test skips whenever the object is packed, then on a store that always packs (the exact CI condition the report blames), the missing-object / fail-closed behaviour is never exercised and the test goes green without running what it guards.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb8705f3f081fd5be","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, first bullet ('or skips with a stated reason when the object is packed') vs third bullet ('proven against BOTH storage shapes')","norm_id":"nd41ee3b94e66058c","priority":0.67,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A CI store that packs the ticket blob before the assertion: test SKIPS, reports green, and the pinned-view-fails-closed behaviour is never verified — reproducing the original 'behaviour never executed' defect the plan set out to remove."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Delete the object via a storage-agnostic route (e.g. remove it from both loose and pack storage, or construct the missing-object condition without relying on unlinking a loose file) and force-exercise each shape (pack the repo in one parametrization, keep it loose in the other), asserting PinnedTicketViewError in both — never skip.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State a deterministic method to force the packed-object precondition in the test (e.g. run `git repack -ad` / `git gc` on the store before removal) so the packed shape is provably exercised.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.4687,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC3: 'proven against BOTH storage shapes — object loose, and object packed'","Plan notes packing 'was not reproduced locally' — the packed state is exactly the shape that is hard to force"],"finding":"AC3 requires proving the fix against a PACKED object, but the plan gives no deterministic method to construct the packed-object precondition. Without a stated way to force packing (e.g. `git repack` / `git gc`), the packed-shape assertion cannot be reliably exercised in CI and the criterion is not verifiable on demand.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3c0e79bd6873762d","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria AC3 / Definition of Done 'Both storage shapes exercised'","norm_id":"n583840afd1119915","priority":0.4813,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Test author cannot deterministically create a packed object, so the packed-shape branch is never actually run","'Both shapes exercised' is asserted but has no reproducible construction step"],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"Add a step that explicitly packs the object (`git repack -ad` or `git gc --prune=now`) before removing it, so the packed branch runs deterministically rather than depending on ambient gc timing.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"lo